## 4. Slice summary

Within the pasted proofs, the answer to Asvin’s mathematical question is favorable: every load-bearing local derivation is expressed through an abstract finite residue-field tower, monic division, discrete valuation/Newton/residual-polynomial arithmetic, and completeness/realization interfaces. None uses characteristic zero, finite \(v(p)\), oddness, Witt coordinates, separability of arbitrary fraction-field irreducibles, or field division by ramification indices. The \(F_q[[t]]\) cells are therefore not exceptional for any argument visible in this slice. However, the slice alone does not fully certify the global all-\(O\) conclusion: J-B’s GMN `HigherNewton` citations and J-C’s FGMN citations do not reproduce the publications’ base-valued-field hypotheses, and numerous construction/dictionary results leave the slice as explicit interfaces. No new local mathematics is indicated; what remains is source-scope and interface verification.

